<title>GERMANY: Buba's Zeitler see 1998 German GDP above 97 levels.</title>
<headline>Buba's Zeitler see 1998 German GDP above 97 levels.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Franz-Christoph Zeitler said on Tuesday he was confident that 1998 gross domestic product (GDP) growth in Germany would be somewhat above 1997's levels.</p>
<p>Zeitler added that he considered a growth rate of 2.5 percent in 1997 was attainable.</p>
<p>The Bundesbank official also said the three percent deficit to GDP ratio called for in the Maastricht Treaty for European economic and monetary union (EMU) should be strictly and sustainably met.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
